// XFAIL: RT-186: deref coercion from a program's type to an unsized target is refused: `&w` as `&[i64]` / `&mut [i64]` with Deref<Target = [i64]>, `&t` as `&str` with Deref<Target = str> (0.30.2)
// rustc prints the EXPECT lines (twin: r302d_016_deref_coercion_to_unsized_target.rs.txt).
// vole: `expected '&[i64]', got '&W'` (lines 47, 48), `expected '&mut [i64]', got
// '&mut W'` (49), `expected '&str', got '&T'` (52, 53). A sized Target (i64,
// [i64; 2]) coerces, `&*w` works, and Vec/String coerce to &[T]/&str; only a
// program's Deref to [T] or str is not followed at a coercion site. Since
// v0.28.0 (the g302probe build the same).
// EXPECT: 3 6
// EXPECT: [0, 2, 3]
// EXPECT: héllo 6
use std::ops::{Deref, DerefMut};

struct W {
    a: [i64; 3],
}

impl Deref for W {
    type Target = [i64];

    fn deref(&self) -> &[i64] {
        &self.a
    }
}

impl DerefMut for W {
    fn deref_mut(&mut self) -> &mut [i64] {
        &mut self.a
    }
}

struct T {
    s: &'static str,
}

impl Deref for T {
    type Target = str;

    fn deref(&self) -> &str {
        self.s
    }
}

fn total(s: &[i64]) -> i64 {
    s.iter().sum()
}

fn zero(s: &mut [i64]) {
    s[0] = 0;
}

fn n(s: &str) -> usize {
    s.len()
}

fn main() {
    let mut w = W { a: [1, 2, 3] };
    let s: &[i64] = &w;
    println("{} {}", s.len(), total(&w));
    zero(&mut w);
    println("{:?}", w.a);
    let t = T { s: "héllo" };
    let u: &str = &t;
    println("{} {}", u, n(&t));
}
